## PROVABLY SAFE — D57 and D115, linear family only (the argument)
The linear family needs an m with BOTH (a) 2m > reach, so the deciding (x-1)^2/2 escapes the
walker, and (b) m <= MAX_SCALE, so x = 1 +- 10^-m is representable at the cell.
  D57:  reach 120 -> (a) needs m >= 61; MAX_SCALE = 56 -> (b) needs m <= 56. Empty.
  D115: reach 248 -> (a) needs m >= 125; MAX_SCALE = 114 -> (b) needs m <= 114. Empty.
Both intervals are empty, so the family CANNOT BE INSTANTIATED at these tiers -- a proof, not
an absence of evidence. SCOPE: this proves only that THIS family cannot reach these tiers. It
is NOT a correctness proof for ln_series at D57/D115 against any other family.

